 "product_type": "forecast",
 "bottom_line": "<p>Fresh snow means you could trigger avalanches above treeline. Look for and avoid spots where winds drift the new snow. Those spots will be just below ridgelines, along gully walls, or around terrain features like rock outcrops. Because wind speeds with this storm are light, the drifted snow may be softer and less obvious than the typical Colorado wind slab. Most slopes near and below treeline lack enough snow to produce an avalanche.</p>",
